:: R1_Bedroom_Approach [r1 story]
<<set $time.period = "night">>
<<scene "Bedroom" "files/images/locations/apartment_bedroom_night.png">>
<<objective "End the day.">>

The bedroom is dark except for the glow of Lena's phone. She's lying on her side, scrolling. Her face in that blue light looks younger, softer, like the Lena I met at that gallery opening five years ago, the one who argued with me about Rothko for twenty minutes and then kissed me in the parking lot.

I undress in the dark. Fold my shirt. Hang my slacks. Place my shoes side by side near the closet. Every night, the same geometry of removal.

I slide into bed. The sheets are cool on my side because no one has been warming them. Her side radiates heat. The distance between us is maybe eighteen inches but I have to build up to crossing it the way someone builds up to jumping off a diving board. Not because I'm afraid of her. Because I'm afraid of the answer if the answer is no.

I put my hand on her thigh. Over the blanket. Tentative. The opening move of a chess game I already know the outcome of.

She puts her phone down.

