:: R1_Choice_B [r1 story]
<<modstat "marriageBond" -3>>
<<set $flags.suggestedNew = true>>

<<sayself>>We could try something different.<</sayself>>

She turns her head on the pillow. In the dark I can't read her expression but I can feel it. That slight tension in the air between two people when one of them has said something unexpected.

<<say "Lena">>Different how?<</say>>

I don't have a good answer. I don't even know what I mean. Something. Anything that doesn't feel like photocopying the same act and filing it under "marriage maintenance." But the words don't organize themselves fast enough, and into the gap, her discomfort flows like water.

<<say "Lena">>Daniel, I'm really tired.<</say>>

<<sayself>>No, I know. Forget it.<</sayself>>

<<say "Lena">>It's not that I don't want to, it's just...<</say>>

<<sayself>>It's fine.<</sayself>>

She adjusts her pillow. The conversation curls up and dies between us like a cigarette nobody's smoking. I lie there and listen to her breathing slow down and I wonder what "different" would even look like. I don't have the imagination for it. My father didn't raise me to have imagination. He raised me to have routines.

I look at the nightstand in the dark, at the chip in its paint, small and unfixed and completely indifferent to any of this.

