    <<link "Continue" "R1_PostSex">><</link>>
</div>

:: R1_Choice_C [r1 story]
<<set $flags.acceptedRoutine = true>>

I don't say anything. She picks up her phone. The blue light returns. The chip in the nightstand is right where I left it.

This is what marriage becomes. This is what everyone says and what nobody questions and what I tell myself on nights like this when the distance between her side of the bed and mine feels measured in years rather than inches. This is normal. This is fine. People who've been married for four years don't rip each other's clothes off. They perform maintenance. They check the box. They stare at a chip in the paint and call it enough.

I close my eyes. Sleep takes a long time to arrive, and when it does, it brings no dreams worth remembering.

